<title>SINGAPORE: SMB United says baffled by stock activity.</title>
<headline>SMB United says baffled by stock activity.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switchgear maker SMB United had no idea what could be fuelling hectic activity in its shares, the group's financial controller said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're not aware of any developments that could be affecting the stock,&quot; Tan Ngiap Hong told Reuters by the telephone.</p>
<p>The stock, which was up Singapore $0.03 at S$0.375, topped the actives with a massive 28.2 million shares traded on Friday. About 14 million shares were traded at S$0.375. Dealers said a major fund could be involved.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703083)</p>
